  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Frost Advisories are no longer in effect.\n\nTemperatures are warming into the 40s. Therefore, the Frost\nAdvisories are no longer in effect.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Dry weather continues and above normal \ntemperatures are expected for much of the week into the start of\nthe weekend.\n\nAs what has been the case for the past week or so, dry weather \nis expected to prevail over the next 5-7 days. However this \ntime, above-normal temperatures for late October/early November \nare expected to be accompanied by this dry stretch. \n\nSurface high pressure will largely be in control through much \nof the week, however there will be one dry cold front that is \nprogged to cross through the area tonight into Tuesday. From \nTuesday and beyond, expansive high pressure is expected to \ndominate as upper level ridging develops over the majority of \nthe Central-Eastern CONUS with positive 500 mb anomalies. \n\nAll in all, generally expect highs in the 65 to 70 degree range\ntoday through Wednesday with highs stepping up into the low to \nmid 70s Thursday through Saturday and possibly Sunday.",
